STEP 9.3c: `InsertionLock`, `EchoHold`
(Phase 9 terminal_session, run 3, plan step 3)

First two sub-entities of the aggregate, built test-first and adopted by the legacy `Session` at once. `InsertionLock` (the legacy field `lock: Option<(Instant, Instant, String, String)>` = deadline, cap, expected buffer, buffer before) with `LockSettlement`, and `EchoHold` (`unechoed`, `echo_pending`, `held`, `held_at`: what the wrapper has typed ahead of the shell's echo and the keys held back). `Session` replaces its five fields by `lock: Option<InsertionLock>` and `echo: EchoHold`; the legacy method bodies keep their order (settle, release and consume exactly as `refresh` / `release_held` / `note_forwarded` do today). `poke_lock_due` and `poke_hold_due` (9.0c helpers) are the only characterisation lines that change. Two commits plus optional refactor commits.

READ FIRST (binding as if written here; where this brief and the research differ, this brief with its run's SINCE preamble wins)
- docs/hexagonal-refactor/agent-brief.md: the contract of the refactor (behaviour must not change, tests are locked, how to move code). Three of its lines are SUPERSEDED: the repo is /home/user/tabsmith (Linux, bash; the macOS notes about zsh and aarch64 do not apply); the branch is `refactor/hexagonal-dropdown-terminal-session` (stay on it, never switch, never commit on main); every commit ends with the two trailer lines given in COMMITS below (the Opus line is wrong). Its "gate >= 283 passed, clippy <= 3" is superseded by the numbers below.
- AGENTS.md: load the skills xp-tdd, testing-standard, coding-standards and hexagonal-architecture with the Skill tool BEFORE touching code, and commit when the step is done.
- The Phase 9 research: docs/hexagonal-refactor/phase-9-terminal-session.md (copied there at launch from target/hexagonal-refactor/p9/phase-9-terminal-session.md; read the target/ path if the docs/ copy is missing). The traps (P9-T..), decisions (R..), signatures, test moves and new tests this step needs are quoted below VERBATIM; read the design document's "Module map" and the sections the step cites when you need more. The six area notes behind it stay in target/hexagonal-refactor/p9/ (recon-tracker-domain.md, recon-tracker-infra.md, recon-session-domain.md, recon-use-cases.md, recon-driver-cli.md, recon-governance.md) with their compiled prototypes (recon-*-prototype/): implementers LIFT from them, test-first, they are not drop-ins (they may carry shortcuts such as `SessionId::new(..).expect(..)` or older names; the design document wins over them).
- docs/hexagonal-refactor-plan.md sections 1, 2, 4 (terminal_session), 5 (Phase 9) and docs/ubiquitous-language.md (terminal_session rows) for naming; docs/hexagonal-refactor/source-map/{pty,tracker,cli,types}.md for the original traps (their line numbers are af1b304, the design document's are 5efb4b2, yours are HEAD: always find code by SYMBOL with grep; a line number in this brief is only a hint).

