TEST-FIRST SEAMS (xp-tdd, testing-standard)
- A NEW seam (new type, function or port with behaviour) is built test-first: write the `should_` tests (AAA layout, in-memory fakes or real objects, NO mocks), see them fail for the right reason (RED), write the minimal code (GREEN), run the gate, COMMIT; then clean up (REFACTOR) and COMMIT again when anything changed. A pure move needs no new test (the moved tests and the characterisation fixtures are the net).
- Before writing a new test name run `grep -rn "fn <name>(" src` (it must be empty: testlock keys tests by fn name over the whole tree and a duplicate is a DUPLICATE failure). Use exactly the names in the NEW TESTS table below unless the table says the step chooses the name.
- Test code inside `#[cfg(test)]` modules may use serde_json fixtures and wire real adapters (D2); production domain code uses std + unicode_width only, application code no infrastructure and no external crate (the fitness test checks this since 9.0a).
